    "updated_at": "2017-07-04T10:25:11Z",
    "body": "It seems that the CSS Display level 3 spec already has it. The \"Appendix B: Effects of display: contents on Unusual Elements\" [currently states](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display/#unbox-html):\r\n\r\n> button\r\n> details\r\n> fieldset\r\n> These elements don’t have any special behavior; `display: contents` simply removes their principal box, and their contents _render as normal_.\r\n\r\nAnd it even seems to work in the latest Chrome behind the \"Experimental Web Platform features\" flag (see [jsfiddle](https://jsfiddle.net/39h74fdj/5/)).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/312838093/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
