    "created_at": "2017-07-15T17:01:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-15T17:01:35Z",
    "body": "> what people are really looking for here is to make a <legend> inside a fieldset not have the \"rendered legend\" behavior, right?\r\n\r\n@bzbarsky, IMO, not only that. There are other peculiarities in the `fieldset` behavior that are not always wanted (e.g. content-depending minimum width or new block formatting context regardless the styling). So I suppose that making `fieldset` behave like a usual element would have its use cases by itself. Making `legend` not have the \"rendered legend\" behavior without changing the behavior of `fieldset` would also have its use cases, so probably there should exist an independent solution for this. And what are the problems of the [current definition](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#rendered-legend) of the rendered legend in HTML?",
